  "question": {
    "html": "<p>The table below shows the approximate nuclear radius for a nucleus of carbon-12 <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\left({ }_{6}^{12} \\mathrm{C}\\right)\"></span> and an unknown isotope <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"X\"></span>.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Nucleus</th><th>Nuclear radius / <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\mathrm{m}\"></span></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Carbon-12</td><td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2.7 \\times 10^{-15}\"></span></td></tr><tr><td>Isotope <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"X\"></span></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"5.4 \\times 10^{-15}\"></span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Which of the following is the most likely mass number for isotope <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"X\"></span>?</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\">24</li><li data-label=\"B\">48</li><li data-label=\"C\">84</li><li data-label=\"D\">96</li></ol>"
